On Wednesday evening I am walking home.
On the way, I stop at a small grocery store.
I need specific spices for my dinner this weekend.
The shop is quiet and smells like cumin and chili.
I look at the shelves and find exactly the right spices.
I take three small jars and go to the till.
The shopkeeper greets me in a friendly way.
"Good evening."
"Good evening," I answer.
"Is that everything?" he asks.
"Yes, that is everything, thank you," I answer.
He scans the jars.
"That will be eight Euro fifty, please," he says.
I pay with my card.
"Do you need the receipt?" the shopkeeper asks.
"No, thank you," I say.
I pack the jars carefully into my backpack.
"Have a nice evening," he says.
"Thank you, you too," I answer and leave the shop.
The evening air is still warm.
I walk on to the flat.
